---
title: "What's Actually in My Con Photography Bag"
description: "The real packing list after a dozen conventions — not the gear I wish I used, the gear I do."
pubDate: 2026-04-02
tags: ["photography"]
---

Every con I get asked what I'm shooting with. Here's the honest answer, gear that survives being crammed into a hotel backpack between hallway photoshoots and 2am dance floor sets.

## Body and lenses

A single mirrorless body and two lenses cover 90% of a con weekend: a fast prime for dealer den candids and low dance-floor light, and a short zoom for group fursuit shots where you can't always back up far enough.

## The stuff nobody mentions

- A spare battery lives in a pocket, not the bag — you will get asked for "one more shot" the second you sit down to swap it
- Lens cloth, always, because fursuiters run warm and mesh eyes fog
- A small LED panel for hallway shots where the con center lighting turns everyone orange

## The actual workflow

Cull hard the same night while the con is still happening. Nobody remembers the 40 near-identical frames — they remember the one you post before breakfast.
